Article 5 To apply for a lawyer's practice, a person shall meet the following requirements:
(1) upholding the Constitution of the People's Republic of China;
(2) passing the national uniform legal professional qualification examination and obtaining legal professional qualifications;
(3) having completed a one-year internship at a law firm;
(4) having good character.
The certificates of the national uniform judicial examination and the lawyer qualification credentials obtained before the implementation of the national uniform legal professional qualification examination shall have the same effect as the national uniform legal professional qualification certificate.

Article 6 To apply for a lawyer's practice, the applicant shall submit an application to the judicial administration department of the people's government of a city divided into districts or of a district of a municipality directly under the Central Government, and shall submit the following materials:
(1) the national uniform legal professional qualification certificate;
(2) the certificate issued by the lawyers association certifying that the applicant has passed the internship assessment;
(3) the identity certificate of the applicant;
(4) the certificate issued by the law firm certifying its consent to accept the applicant.
If the applicant applies for part-time lawyer practice, he/she shall also submit a certificate from his/her employer evidencing its consent to the applicant's part-time engagement in the lawyer profession.
The department that accepts the application shall, within twenty days from the date of acceptance, conduct a review and submit the review opinion together with all application materials to the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government. The judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government shall, within ten days from the date of receiving the submitted materials, conduct an examination and make a decision on whether to grant the practice. If the practice is granted, a lawyer's practice certificate shall be issued to the applicant; if not, a written explanation shall be provided to the applicant.

Article 7 A lawyer's practice certificate shall not be issued under any of the following circumstances of the applicant:
(1) having no capacity for civil conduct or having limited capacity for civil conduct;
(2) having been subjected to criminal punishment, except for crimes of negligence;
(3) having been discharged from public employment or having his/her lawyer's or notary's practice certificate revoked.

Article 9 Under any of the following circumstances, the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government shall revoke the decision to permit practice and cancel the lawyer's practice certificate of the person who has been permitted to practice:
(1) the applicant obtained the lawyer's practice certificate by fraud, bribery or other improper means;
(2) the applicant was permitted to practice despite not meeting the requirements prescribed by this Law.

Article 14 A law firm is the practice institution for lawyers. The establishment of a law firm shall meet the following requirements:
(1) having its own name, domicile and articles of association;
(2) having lawyers meeting the requirements of this Law;
(3) the founder(s) shall be a lawyer(s) with certain practice experience and no punishment of suspension from practice within the preceding three years;
(4) having assets in an amount prescribed by the judicial administration department of the State Council.

Article 17 To apply for the establishment of a law firm, the following materials shall be submitted:
(1) a written application;
(2) the name and articles of association of the law firm;
(3) the list of lawyers, their resumes, identity certificates and lawyer practice certificates;
(4) proof of domicile;
(5) proof of assets.
To establish a partnership law firm, a partnership agreement shall also be submitted.

Article 22 A law firm shall be terminated under any of the following circumstances:
(1) It fails to maintain the statutory conditions for establishment and still fails to meet the conditions after rectification within a prescribed time limit;
(2) Its practice license is revoked according to law;
(3) It decides to dissolve on its own;
(4) Other circumstances under which termination shall occur as provided by laws and administrative regulations.
Where a law firm is terminated, the department that issued its practice license shall cancel the practice license of the law firm.

Article 28 A lawyer may engage in the following business:
(1) Accepting entrustment from natural persons, legal persons, or other organizations to serve as legal advisers;
(2) Accepting entrustment from parties in civil cases and administrative cases to serve as agents ad litem and participate in litigation;
(3) Accepting entrustment from criminal suspects or defendants in criminal cases or accepting designation from legal aid institutions according to law to serve as defenders, and accepting entrustment from private prosecutors in cases of private prosecution, victims in cases of public prosecution or their close relatives to serve as agents ad litem and participate in litigation;
(4) Accepting entrustment to represent clients in petitions for various litigation cases;
(5) Accepting entrustment to participate in mediation and arbitration activities;
(6) Accepting entrustment to provide non-litigation legal services;
(7) Answering inquiries concerning law, drafting litigation documents and other documents concerning legal matters.

Article 40 A lawyer shall not commit any of the following acts in his or her practice activities:
(1) Privately accepting entrustment or collecting fees, or accepting property or other benefits from a client;
(2) Taking advantage of the convenience of providing legal services to seek the rights and interests disputed by the parties;
(3) Accepting property or other benefits from the opposing party, maliciously colluding with the opposing party or a third party to infringe upon the rights and interests of the client;
(4) Meeting with judges, prosecutors, arbitrators, or other relevant staff members in violation of regulations;
(5) Offering bribes to judges, prosecutors, arbitrators, or other relevant staff members, introducing bribes, or instructing or inducing parties to offer bribes, or otherwise improperly influencing judges, prosecutors, arbitrators, or other relevant staff members in handling cases according to law;
(6) Intentionally providing false evidence, or threatening or inducing others to provide false evidence, or hindering the opposing party from lawfully obtaining evidence;
(7) Inciting or instigating parties to resolve disputes by illegal means such as disrupting public order or endangering public security;
(8) Disrupting court or arbitration tribunal order, or interfering with the normal progress of litigation or arbitration activities.

Article 46 A lawyers association shall perform the following duties:
(1) ensuring that lawyers practice law according to law and safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of lawyers;
(2) summarizing and exchanging experience in the work of lawyers;
(3) formulating industry regulations and disciplinary rules;
(4) organizing professional training for lawyers and education on professional ethics and practice discipline, and conducting assessment of lawyers' practice activities;
(5) organizing and managing the internship activities of applicants for lawyer practice licenses, and assessing interns;
(6) imposing rewards and disciplinary sanctions on lawyers and law firms;
(7) accepting complaints or reports against lawyers, mediating disputes arising from lawyers' practice activities, and accepting petitions from lawyers;
(8) other duties as provided by laws, administrative regulations, rules, and the articles of association of the lawyers association.
The industry regulations and disciplinary rules formulated by a lawyers association shall not conflict with relevant laws, administrative regulations, and rules.

Article 47 Where a lawyer commits any of the following acts, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a city divided into districts or of a district of a municipality directly under the Central Government shall issue a warning and may impose a fine of not more than 5,000 yuan; if there are illegal gains, such gains shall be confiscated; if the circumstances are serious, a penalty of suspension from practice for not more than three months shall be imposed:
(1) practicing law in two or more law firms simultaneously;
(2) soliciting business by illegitimate means;
(3) acting as agent for both parties in the same case, or handling legal matters in which there is a conflict of interest with the lawyer himself or his close relatives;
(4) acting as a litigation agent or defender within two years after leaving the People's Court or the People's Procuratorate;
(5) refusing to fulfill the obligation of legal aid.

Article 48 Where a lawyer commits any of the following acts, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a city divided into districts or of a district of a municipality directly under the Central Government shall issue a warning and may impose a fine of not more than 10,000 yuan; if there are illegal gains, such gains shall be confiscated; if the circumstances are serious, a penalty of suspension from practice for not less than three months but not more than six months shall be imposed:
(1) accepting a commission or charging fees privately, or accepting property or other benefits from the client;
(2) after accepting a commission, refusing to defend or represent without justifiable reasons, or failing to appear in court on time to participate in litigation or arbitration;
(3) taking advantage of the convenience of providing legal services to seek the rights and interests in dispute of the parties;
(4) disclosing trade secrets or personal privacy.

Article 49 Where a lawyer commits any of the following acts, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a city divided into districts or of a district of a municipality directly under the Central Government shall impose a penalty of suspension from practice for not less than six months but not more than one year, and may impose a fine of not more than 50,000 yuan; if there are illegal gains, such gains shall be confiscated; if the circumstances are serious, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall revoke his lawyer's practice certificate; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) meeting with judges, prosecutors, arbitrators, or other relevant staff in violation of regulations, or otherwise improperly influencing the handling of cases according to law;
(2) offering bribes to judges, prosecutors, arbitrators, or other relevant staff, introducing bribes, or instructing or inducing the parties to offer bribes;
(3) providing false materials to the judicial administration department or engaging in other fraudulent acts;
(4) intentionally providing false evidence or threatening or inducing others to provide false evidence, or hindering the opposing party from lawfully obtaining evidence;
(5) accepting property or other benefits from the opposing party, or maliciously colluding with the opposing party or a third party to infringe upon the rights of the client;
(6) disrupting the order of the court or arbitral tribunal, or interfering with the normal progress of litigation or arbitration activities;
(7) inciting or instigating the parties to resolve disputes by illegal means such as disturbing public order or endangering public safety;
(8) making statements that endanger national security, maliciously defame others, or seriously disrupt the order of the court;
(9) disclosing state secrets.
Where a lawyer is subject to criminal punishment for intentional crime, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall revoke his lawyer's practice certificate.

Article 50 Where a law firm commits any of the following acts, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a city divided into districts or of a district of a municipality directly under the Central Government shall, depending on the circumstances, impose a penalty of warning or suspension for rectification for not less than one month but not more than six months, and may impose a fine of not more than 100,000 yuan; if there are illegal gains, such gains shall be confiscated; if the circumstances are especially serious, the judicial administration department of the people's government of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall revoke the law firm's practice certificate:
(1) accepting commissions or charging fees in violation of regulations;
(2) handling major matters such as changing the name, responsible person, articles of association, partnership agreement, address, or partners in violation of statutory procedures;
(3) engaging in business activities other than legal services;
(4) soliciting business by illegitimate means such as slandering other law firms or lawyers, or paying referral fees;
(5) accepting cases with conflicts of interest in violation of regulations;
(6) refusing to fulfill the obligation of legal aid;
(7) providing false materials to the judicial administration department or engaging in other fraudulent acts;
(8) failing to properly supervise the lawyers of the firm, causing serious consequences.
Where a law firm is penalized for the illegal acts mentioned in the preceding paragraph, its responsible person shall, depending on the seriousness of the circumstances, be given a warning or be imposed a fine of not more than 20,000 yuan.
